      "widgets_values": [
        "Chinese wuxia film opening, adult characters, cinematic live action. <Picture 1> defines the heroine's face, hair, ivory and pale-blue hanfu and the ancient pavilion in a bamboo grove. Keep her identity and costume consistent. Animate full body actions with clear intent, weight, foot placement and readable gestures. Real spatial movement, not a still portrait with moving hair. One continuous shot with the camera movement specified below. No internal cuts, captions, logos, modern objects or extra limbs. Silent video.\nSHOT 3 — FIRST CLASH. <Picture 2> is the previous shot's final frame. Continue the same heroine and dark-robed adult rival, their swords, positions and bamboo path. A readable short wuxia exchange over about ten seconds: first the rival steps forward and delivers one diagonal sword strike; the heroine steps sideways and raises her blade to parry, the blades visibly meeting once. Then she pivots on her planted foot and makes a single controlled horizontal counterstrike; he steps back and blocks it. Finally they disengage by one step and hold opposing guard stances, leaving a tense ending for a title added later. Camera: a controlled low lateral tracking move during the exchange, then gently pull back to a wider view at the end. Full bodies and blade paths remain visible. Grounded footwork, fast decisive actions separated by short readable pauses; no flying, no spinning camera, no gore. Exactly two people.",
        960,
        544,
        243,
        "match"
      ],
